              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kizer Shelton"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe! Being a pescotarian its hard to find good recipes. Although i would add a little bit of lemon juice, too. thank u for this recipe!!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Opal Stephanie Barrett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved it! I used Mahi Mahi instead of shrimp, &amp; pineapple as well as mango. I also added a Serano pepper which was probably a mistake. I wonder if I should have rinsed the Mahi Mahi off after it was “cooked“. One recommendation or one point I would make is that the last thing you should add is avocado right before you’re ready to serve as the dish seem to sweat and produce a lot of liquid. I really felt like it wasn’t good past that evening and threw most of it away but other than that it was phenomenal and I will definitely make it again!",
            "datePublished": "2018-08-31T17:30:10.247Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Leslie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have never written a review, however this dish was EXCELLENT! I made it as an appetizer for Easter, and it was the hit of my dinner party! I cut up my raw shrimp and marinated over night in fresh lemon and lime juice. I drained and dropped them in boiling water for a few minutes until cooked, and drained. This gave the shrimp a nice flavor! I followed the recipe after that,leaving out the avocado. I served them with tortilla chips and the avocado on the side. I made 3 pounds of shrimp and they were scraping the bowl for more!\n\nBeautiful presentation!",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-05T07:51:52.183Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "czarria60"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I’ve made lots of ceviches and my favorite shrimp ceviche is a lot different than this recipe and has more of a cocktail sauce base to it, but I was looking for something a little lighter for a lunch with friends. This sounded good and fresh. I wasn’t disappointed. I followed the recipe exactly except that I added about 1/4 c of ketchup. Don’t knock it til you try it. It adds just a bit more sweetness that works with this recipe. My dear FIL, who was a ceviche maker all his life, swore by good ole ketchup!! Anyway, this is a great recipe and I’ll use again!!",
            "datePublished": "2019-10-24T14:29:41.907Z"
          },
          {
